  "_comment": "PHASE 9 recovery item 14A. Node ids used by shipping .zlogic assets that have no definition in the catalogue at all -- measured on the NORMALIZED graph, so node-id aliases are already applied. These nodes load, produce nothing, and their edges are dead. This file bounds the class: the gate fails on any NEW id and on any recorded id that stops being phantom, so the set cannot grow or rot silently. Item 14A restored exactly one id, object.find_by_name, which had historical evidence; everything here is deliberately NOT restored. Crucially, the ids in 'never_implemented' are NOT lost runtime: a search across every commit found no definition and no executor for them, ever. They are new design work, and treating them as recovery would be inventing semantics.",
